---
import { comparison } from '../../lib/comparison';

// What CostCook connects to, on /features rather than on a page of its own.
//
// WHY NOT A DEDICATED PAGE. Two Coming rows and one shipped argument is not a
// page; a page of nothing but Coming reads as a roadmap and costs trust with
// the exact reader this site is built for. It becomes its own route when there
// are four shipped connections to put on it, not before.
//
// THE ORDER IS THE ARGUMENT. Competitors lead an integrations page with logos.
// The honest thing CostCook has and they do not is that prices arrive without
// a connection at all, because the intake reads the paper the supplier already
// sends. So that goes first and the two in-flight connectors go second, where
// they read as additions rather than as the answer.
//
// EVIDENCE. Five doors is RC-38, read on sandbox/demo: the import dropzone
// accepts JPEG, PNG, WebP, PDF, CSV, XLSX and DOCX, with a paste control
// beside it. Staged-until-confirmed is RC-09. The unreadable note is RC-39.
// Square and QuickBooks are RC-45. QuickBooks is genuinely unbuilt. Square is
// NOT: sandbox/demo carries the provider, catalog mapping, settings screens,
// the OAuth callback and the webhook, all of it behind
// integrationExecutionAllowed(businessId, 'square_integration',
// env.FEATURE_SQUARE_INTEGRATION_ENABLED), which defaults off. "Coming" is
// therefore true of the app a reader would start today and stays true only
// while that flag is off in production. If it is ever switched on for anyone,
// this section and the /compare row are both underclaiming and must move to
// Yes. Neither carries a date either way.
//
// The two Coming lines are read out of comparison.ts rather than retyped, so
// the /compare table and this section cannot say different things about the
// same connector.
const comingRows = comparison
	.flatMap((group) => group.rows)
	.filter((row) => row.label === 'Point of sale' || row.label === 'Accounting');
---

<section id="connections" class="border-t border-hairline" aria-labelledby="connections-heading">
	<div class="container-page py-section">
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<p class="eyebrow">What it connects to</p>
			<h2 id="connections-heading" class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">
				Your supplier does not have to be plugged in. CostCook reads the paper.
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-5 max-w-[62ch] text-lede text-ink-soft">
				The reason there is no long list of connectors here is that prices get in
				without one. An order guide, a price sheet, an invoice, or a photograph of a
				delivery slip taken on the loading dock all go through the same queue.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 border-y border-ticket-rule py-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
			<div>
				<h3 class="font-semibold">Five doors in</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
					A photo, a PDF, a spreadsheet, a Word document, or text you paste. Every one
					lands in the same review.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="font-semibold">Staged, not written</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
					What comes out sits outside your catalog until you confirm it. Nothing
					reaches a plate cost that you have not seen.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="font-semibold">What it could not read</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
					Anything unreadable is quoted back to you word for word, beside what was
					staged, rather than dropped or guessed at.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
			<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold">Two connections, at two different distances</h3>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-[62ch] text-ink-soft">
				Coming means the same here as it does on the comparison page: not in the app
				you would start today. It does not mean these two are at the same stage, and
				the lines below say which is which. There is no date on either, because a date
				is a promise and neither has earned one yet.
			</p>
			<ul role="list" class="mt-6 space-y-5">
				{
					comingRows.map((row) => (
						<li class="border-t border-hairline pt-4">
							<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
								<p class="font-semibold">{row.label}</p>
								<span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-ticket-rule bg-softamber px-2.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-amber-deep">
									Coming
								</span>
							</div>
							<p class="mt-2 max-w-[62ch] text-ink-soft">{row.note}</p>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ul>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-[62ch] text-sm text-ink-soft">
				Until they land, nothing in CostCook reads from or writes to your books or your
				till.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
